<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom ADRs up US$3-3/4 as Dow eases.</title>
<headline>Telecom ADRs up US$3-3/4 as Dow eases.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom was up US$3-3/4 in New York trade but other ADRs were mixed as the Dow retreated 10.44 to 5999.57 in late trade at 7.45 am NZT (1845 GMT).</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company     Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$27 1/8	 +1</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$26 3/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 7/8	 -0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16 1/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$82	     +3 3/4</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$14 1/4	  NIL</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33 3/4	    -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		 untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  241 1/2	   +3</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  156 1/2	   +1</p>
<p>Templeton	London  140 1/2	   +0</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.18	    +3</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.51	    +3</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.12	    -3</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
